---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={`About Our Editorial Process | ${SITE_TITLE}`} description="Learn how we source, review, and verify peer-reviewed health research and medical news." />
		<style>
			:root {
				--bg-root: #1a222d;
				--bg-raised: #212b38;
				--border: rgba(206, 220, 235, 0.12);
				--border-strong: rgba(206, 220, 235, 0.22);
				--text-main: #e9eef4;
				--text-body: #c3cedb;
				--text-muted: #92a1b3;
				--accent: #7fd6c2;
				--accent-strong: #a6e8d8;
				--accent-soft: rgba(127, 214, 194, 0.12);
				--serif: 'Iowan Old Style', 'Palatino Linotype', Palatino, Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;
				--sans: system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;
			}

			*, *::before, *::after {
				box-sizing: border-box;
			}

			body {
				background-color: var(--bg-root);
				background-image: linear-gradient(180deg, #202a37 0%, var(--bg-root) 520px);
				background-repeat: no-repeat;
				color: var(--text-main);
				font-family: var(--sans);
				margin: 0;
				padding: 0;
				-webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
			}

			main {
				width: 800px;
				max-width: calc(100% - 2rem);
				margin: 0 auto;
				padding: 4rem 0 6rem;
			}

			.page-header {
				margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
				padding-bottom: 2rem;
				border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
			}

			.badge {
				display: inline-flex;
				align-items: center;
				gap: 0.55rem;
				color: var(--accent);
				font-size: 0.9rem;
				font-weight: 500;
				margin-bottom: 1rem;
			}

			.badge-dot {
				width: 8px;
				height: 8px;
				background: var(--accent);
				border-radius: 50%;
				box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px var(--accent-soft);
			}

			h1 {
				font-family: var(--serif);
				font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4.5vw, 3.2rem);
				font-weight: 600;
				line-height: 1.15;
				letter-spacing: -0.025em;
				margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
				color: var(--accent);
			}

			.lead {
				color: var(--text-body);
				font-size: 1.15rem;
				line-height: 1.7;
				margin: 0;
			}

			.content-section {
				margin-bottom: 3rem;
			}

			h2 {
				font-family: var(--serif);
				font-size: 1.75rem;
				font-weight: 600;
				color: var(--text-main);
				margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
				letter-spacing: -0.015em;
			}

			p {
				color: var(--text-body);
				font-size: 1.02rem;
				line-height: 1.75;
				margin: 0 0 1.25rem 0;
			}

			.process-grid {
				display: grid;
				grid-template-columns: 1fr;
				gap: 1.5rem;
				margin: 2rem 0;
			}

			.process-card {
				background: var(--bg-raised);
				border: 1px solid var(--border);
				border-radius: 16px;
				padding: 2rem;
			}

			.process-card h3 {
				font-family: var(--serif);
				font-size: 1.25rem;
				color: var(--accent);
				margin: 0 0 0.75rem 0;
			}

			.process-card p {
				margin: 0;
				font-size: 0.98rem;
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<div class="page-header">
				<div class="badge">
					<span class="badge-dot"></span>
					Editorial Integrity & Standards
				</div>
				<h1>About Our Editorial Process</h1>
				<p class="lead">
					How we translate rigorous peer-reviewed clinical research and medical science into transparent, accessible, and dependable daily intelligence.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="content-section">
				<h2>Our Commitment to Scientific Accuracy</h2>
				<p>
					In an era of rapid information flow, health news requires uncompromising precision. Our publication is structured to eliminate speculation, sensationalism, and unverified health claims. Every briefing we publish is anchored directly in primary source scientific literature.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="process-grid">
				<div class="process-card">
					<h3>1. Primary Source Sourcing</h3>
					<p>
						We monitor major peer-reviewed journals, clinical trial registries, and institutional publications—including PubMed, The Lancet, JAMA, and the New England Journal of Medicine—to identify high-impact medical findings.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="process-card">
					<h3>2. Clinical Verification & Context</h3>
					<p>
						Our editorial team evaluates sample sizes, methodology limitations, and statistical significance. We explicitly distinguish between preliminary observational findings, animal models, and fully randomized controlled trials (RCTs) in human cohorts.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="process-card">
					<h3>3. Plain-Language Translation</h3>
					<p>
						We strip away dense medical jargon without sacrificing technical validity. Our goal is to make complex research metrics understandable and actionable for our readers while strictly preserving the integrity of the original data.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="process-card">
					<h3>4. Ongoing Corrections & Updates</h3>
					<p>
						Science is iterative. If follow-up research, clinical retractions, or data updates modify our understanding of a published briefing, we append transparent correction notes with clear timestamps directly to the article.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="content-section" style="margin-top: 3.5rem;">
				<h2>Editorial Independence</h2>
				<p>
					Our reporting remains strictly independent. Advertisers, ad networks (such as Mediavine), and commercial partners have zero influence over our editorial selection, research coverage, or scientific conclusions.
				</p>
			</div>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
